  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes, especially when sentiment is neutral or negative.",
    "Adjust forecasts downward if recent true outcomes show persistent mean reversion toward lower levels after high peaks.",
    "When sentiment turns negative (e.g., -0.25 or below), reduce forecast volatility and shift toward historical mean or support levels.",
    "If model consistently overestimates prices in early forecast windows (e.g., first 5 days), apply a 5-10% downward bias to mitigate overconfidence.",
    "For sentiment-neutral periods, apply a mild smoothing filter to reduce noise and avoid overreacting to short-term volatility.",
    "In cases where true outcomes dip sharply after a forecast peak, apply a lag correction: reduce forecast by 10-20% for the next 3-5 days to account for delayed market reaction."
